WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.680
Hello everyone and welcome to the Langfocus channel, and my name is Paul.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:09.560
Today this is not a feature video. This is just a special video in which I'm going to make a little announcement

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.260
and then I'm going to answer some frequently asked questions that a lot of people ask me

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.680
in the comments of videos 
and also in private messages.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:23.140
So, the first announcement that I want to make 
is that I have created a Patreon account.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.320
Now maybe you don't know what Patreon is.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.740
Patreon is a service that allows you to basically 
support your favorite YouTube creators by pledging

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.740
to give them a certain amount of money each month.
An amount of money that you decide.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.540
Now I want to say right away: you don't have 
to do this, you don't have to give any money.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.920
This is basically like a voluntary subscription fee 
that you can pay if you want.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.720
But the amount is up to you.
So it can be as little as one dollar.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.260
That's one of the cool things about Patreon 
is that everyone can give us one dollar

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:01.780
Not everyone but if you want, you can give one dollar 
and if a lot of people give one dollar, 
then that amount of money kind of adds up

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.520
And the creator gets you no significant amount. 
So that's the cool thing about it.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.720
It's kind of a collective way to support
your favorite creators as a team.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.880
So the reason I'm doing that is because I put in a lot 
of time and effort into making the videos and...

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:20.180
basically that's a lot of time that I could be putting 
into different work that pays money.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.180
I do get a little bit of money from 
some advertising on Youtube

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.160
But it's just a small amount,
it's not really a lot.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.320
And that's because, according to my statistics, 
about 70% of people use ad blockers.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.920
And that's okay. 
I don't really mind if you do that. That's up to you.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.500
Of course, this is all voluntary. If you want to support
the channel, Patreon is a way to do that.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.760
Even if you like to use an ad blocker 
or whatever things like that.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.160
Basically have a look at the Patreon page
that I've created.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.900
If you think that Langfocus deserves a little donation 
every month, a dollar or whatever you want to give, then...

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:57.260
that would be highly appreciated. But if not, then don't 
worry about it, because I'll still love you just as much.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.720
You'll still be a valued viewer and all of that. 
So don't even stress about it.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.600
It's completely voluntary.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.260
And the link to that Patreon page is 
down below in the description.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.560
So, on to a few frequently asked questions.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.960
So the first frequently asked question is:
Paul, how many languages do you speak?

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.800
Now this is a strange question to be asked 
because it kind of feels like...

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:23.700
because I'm making the videos, that people think 
I'm a language master or a language guru.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.240
or one of those things. And I don't think of myself 
like that. I don't think I'm a language master.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.940
I'm just someone who's very passionate about
languages and very interested in them.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.000
And I'm also very passionate about learning
because I'm a teacher, but also I just love learning.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.160
But I know why people are asking that question. 
So I'll try to give you my answer off.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.660
I'll tell you which languages that I've basically invested 
a lot of time into studying, that I've studied in depth,

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.440
and that I have a significant amount of knowledge of.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.560
It doesn't mean I'm really advanced at those languages 
but it means I put that time and effort into them.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.300
So the first one that I studied, 
back in the day, was Hebrew.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.060
In university, I studied Biblical Hebrew 
but, in my free time, I also studied modern Hebrew

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.140
I also studied Biblical Arameic at university.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.020
And, at the same time, I studied
Old English or Anglo-Saxon

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.780
So we can throw that in there. 
It's not a spoken language but I'll throw that in there.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.980
I've also studied Arabic.
I've studied modern Standard Arabic.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:21.980
And also some Arabic dialects, specifically Palestinian 
and, to some extent, Egyptian as well.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:27.540
I've also, of course, studied Japanese. 
As you might know, I live in Japan 
and I've been studying Japanese for a long time

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.600
I've also studied Indonesian. 
I've also studied French.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.000
I've also studied Tagalog 
I've also studied Esperanto.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.720
And I've also recently been studying Italian.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.860
So those are the ones I've really put time
and effort into studying quite a lot.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.480
I don't know if I'm forgetting any 
but that's probably the main ones.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.940
There are other languages that I've studied to 
a basic level but I don't really know them enough
to say that I know them

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.520
And there are some languages that I can also read.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.100
Like I have passive knowledge of them,
because I've studied related languages.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.500
But I've never specifically studied 
those languages themselves so...

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.880
For example, Portuguese and Spanish, I can...

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.660
I can often make sense of them 
when I'm reading them, but I've never studied them.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:10.500
There are also other languages that 
I just studied from a linguist's point of view.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.700
Like I want to see how those languages work.
So I examined them.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.040
Sometimes the language profile videos 
I make are kind of like that.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:22.420
Like I'm just interested in those languages. 
So I examine them and study 
and learn about those languages.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.800
But I haven't necessarily studied those languages.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.980
Basically, I consider myself a language enthusiast,
 someone who loves languages.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.460
I don't call myself a polyglot.
I'm not going to make a video called:

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.920
"Canadian guy speaks 25 languages" 
or something like that.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.100
Like that's not really the purpose of this channel.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.920
The channel is called Langfocus 
because I want to focus on the languages.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.360
Not really on me and my own ability.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.560
Another frequently asked question I get is: 
"Paul, what do you do for a living? 
Is it related to languages?"

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.980
Well, yes, kind of. I'm an instructor at a university.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.860
And I teach English as a foreign language
to students in Japan.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:01.640
So, originally, part of the reasons I made the Langfocus 
channel was kind of to inspire my students.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:06.040
So I have some videos to show them and I could 
show them that my hobby is language learning.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.700
And I could give them some extra motivation 
to work hard to study English,

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.400
because they could see that 
their teacher is doing that too.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.020
Another frequently asked question I get is:
 "Paul, what's your educational background?"

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.120
Well, I have 2 university degrees.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.940
My first university degree was in English
with a linguistics focus.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.880
So it wasn't a literature degree, it was a linguistics
degree in the English department.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:33.440
So that means I studied the history of English 
I studied English grammar, I studied English phonology,

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:39.680
I studied dialectal differences in English. 
I studied all of those kinds of things 
about the English language.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.040
I also had a minor in religious studies.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:48.640
Basically all of my credits that went towards that minor
were courses in biblical Hebrew and biblical Aramaic.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:53.260
I wanted to study those languages and I figured out 
that I could get a minor in religious studies,

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.640
by just taking those courses.
So that's what I did.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:59.440
I also have a second university degree.
That one is in Education.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:04.260
After I finished my first degree, I went back 
to university and did a second degree in education.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:08.600
And that's what allows me to be a teacher 
and do my current job at the university.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:14.560
So that's just a little bit about me. It seems like 
some of the viewers want to get to know
a little bit more about me personally.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:21.060
If you're one of those people, you can check out 
my Instagram too. That gives you a little bit of 
a glimpse into my life, my daily life.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:26.260
And you can follow me on Facebook as well
and all of those different social media channels.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.080
So thank you for watching. Have a nice day.

